> Checked inputs and owned pipeline outputs

Positive dimensions, exact N*N pixels, matched rectangular sinograms and
nonempty finite angle lists are validated before numerical work/output
allocation. All pixel and projection inputs must be finite. Detector
coordinates outside the supported interpolation range are skipped before
floor-to-int conversion; pixel/kernel/sinogram geometry uses checked sizes.
A finite-input accumulation that becomes nonfinite raises overflow_error.
The original empty-image call produced an invalid read; the original
zero-angle reconstruction returned zeros without projection data. Its
nominal pi/M normalization is undefined at M=0. Both cases now reject as
invalid controls. Standalone filtering accepts an empty
sinogram and returns empty output.

All stage outputs own their buffers. For M views,D detector bins and N × N
pixels, forward storage is O(MD), direct filtering uses O(MD) output plus
O(D) kernel, and gather uses O(N²) output. FBP takes O(MD²+MN²) word
work, with temporary filtered rows and the ordinary output image. These
buffers are actual stage outputs, rather than an optional explanatory
history. There is no capture-record quota, byte-serialization format or
physical calibration implied by the numeric arrays.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fbp_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/filtered_back_projection.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/online_statistics.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <climits>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
