\caption(The checked APIs reject the original unsafe empty-image and empty-angle cases,alongside malformed and nonfinite data. The actual intermediate and final buffers remain independent after caller edits.)
\alttext(A native three-stage diagram shows an eight-by-nine sinogram,eight-by-nine finite filtered rows,and twenty-five owned reconstructed pixels. Executed controls reject invalid geometry and nonfinite arithmetic.)

> Verification and references

The original valid numerical behavior is retained across 60,188 frozen
floating-bit records from 168 small signed-pixel fixtures and the original
64 × 64 and 96 × 96 disk cases, plus all five original full-program output
lines. Ten strict sanitizer cases compare the finite operators against
an independent dense hat-basis matrix and analytical convolution matrix,
check 300 seeded scaled-adjoint/linearity fixtures, shape/finite/capacity
controls, clipping, rounded angles, finite overflow and owned outputs.
The public Doxygen examples compile and their displayed output is checked.

A. C. Kak and M. Slaney,
[Principles of Computerized Tomographic Imaging,chapter3](https://engineering.purdue.edu/~malcolm/pct/CTI_Ch03.pdf),
IEEE Press, 1988,sections 3.1–3.3,especially equations 45 and 61,describe the
parallel-beam geometry,interpolated backprojection and sampled ramp filter.
The native finite pixel splat,zero extension,unit spacing and angular
weights are specified above. Ideal continuous inversion is not a claim
that this finite A-transpose H A equals the identity.

G. N. Ramachandran and A. V. Lakshminarayanan,
[Three-dimensional Reconstruction from Radiographs and Electron Micrographs:
Application of Convolutions instead of Fourier Transforms](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.68.9.2236),
PNAS 68(9), 1971, pp.2236–2240,introduced convolution-based reconstruction.
The native implementation's precise coefficient convention is checked
against Kak and Slaney's sampled unit-spacing expression.
